The theoretical core remains:

• trust in automation;
• human adoption of machine advice;
• algorithm aversion and algorithm appreciation.

2. A few early errors determine whether an entire system continues to use AI

Real-world AI applications often begin as pilots:
• an organization deploys on a small scale;
• users observe early performance;
• the organization decides whether to expand, restrict, or terminate use.

This directly affects monitoring, correction, and exit mechanisms for the AI system.
